The SECURITY.md template is a comprehensive document that outlines security practices and guidelines for software development. Here are some key points:

    Purpose: It serves as the authoritative source for all security practices and guidelines, implementing a security-first development philosophy.
    1
    Content: The template includes sections on vulnerability disclosure, data classification, secrets management, access control, incident response, and more.
    1
    Implementation: It is designed to be a single source of truth for security practices, linking to other meta-files for consistency.
    1
    Versioning: The template is versioned in Git, ensuring changes are tracked and approved via PR.
    1

    For more detailed information, you can refer to the specific templates available on GitHub.

